00:04:37.937 --> 00:04:39.361
I have three quick tips for

00:04:39.361 --> 00:04:44.350
you to help you to differentiate yourself
professionally in the waiting room.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.950
First, try to plan to stand up.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:48.830
Standing up,

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:52.309
based on author Peggy Wallace,
gives you more power and confidence.

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:56.480
Standing up gives you more
energy because it's so

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:00.110
much better than if you would
have slouch in the couch.

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:04.490
We are nervous in an interview,
your default will be to take refuge

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:07.850
in sinking in that comfortable
couch in the waiting room.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:11.540
Instead of sitting there, you can
look out the view out of the window,

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:16.540
read about the art on the wall or read
about a magazine while you're standing.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:20.359
Standing up has one other benefit,
when someone you meet comes in,

00:05:20.359 --> 00:05:24.647
standing up gives you a more fluid
transition into greeting them because you

00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:29.009
stand out as their equal rather than
from below them from a sitting position.

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:35.236
The second tip we have for
you is to make small conversations.

00:05:35.236 --> 00:05:37.690
They can be with people
in the receptionist or

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:40.130
they can be other candidates in the room.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:44.700
This helps you stretch out your vocal
cords so you can deliver a more clear and

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.400
resonant voice.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.940
And hopefully, the admins will see
that you are a friendly person and

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:54.640
you're a better fit for the company's
culture, convert them into your allies.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:00.510
The third tip we have for
you is to master the meet and greet.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.080
You won't be able to immediately
have this high energy

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.920
as soon as you see someone
in that first millisecond.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:12.359
Therefore prepare the mentality for
solid first impression.

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.050
Think about what you
want to do to be confident,

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:19.390
to show enthusiasm and
show that you are polished.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:24.203
Greet them with an open gesture, a firm
handshake, and a direct eye contact.

00:06:24.203 --> 00:06:27.170
Let's practise this.

00:06:27.170 --> 00:06:28.805
&gt;&gt; Hey Tammie.

00:06:28.805 --> 00:06:30.182
&gt;&gt; Much better, isn't it?

00:06:30.182 --> 00:06:33.182
So as you can see,
there are three quick tips for

00:06:33.182 --> 00:06:36.400
you to prepare in the waiting room.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:39.930
As we said,
it really starts before it starts.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.875
&gt;&gt; Now let's talk about preparing
Brett for the interview room.

00:06:45.875 --> 00:06:48.690
Brett, come on in, have a seat.

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:52.270
&gt;&gt; I have three tips for you.

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:58.370
First, have engaging conversation for
your interviewer and prepare for that.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:00.580
Do your homework beforehand.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:02.200
Look up what they work on,

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:06.290
where they went to school or
college, what their hobbies are.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.360
See if you have any
commonalities with them or

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.499
shared experiences,
talk about those to build connections.

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:15.505
Second, let's talk about posture.

00:07:15.505 --> 00:07:19.820
Brett, when you sit with your
leg up against your knee, and

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:25.150
slouching back, you convey a casual
attitude and a bit of arrogance.

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:26.390
Let's fix that.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:29.020
Why don't you sit straight and
try to project confidence.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:34.000
It's important to maintain eye
contact with your interviewer so

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.810
that it builds trust.

00:07:37.090 --> 00:07:39.030
When you look away from
your interviewer and

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:41.270
talk, they might think you
are not being genuine.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:47.010
Third, it is important to
mirror the energy in the room.

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:48.810
Practice this beforehand.

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:51.465
If your interviewer is low energy or
tired,

00:07:51.465 --> 00:07:57.260
don't be too peppy, if your interview is
high energy, try to match their level.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:08:02.410
You want the interviewer to be comfortable
with your energy level and not be awkward.

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:09.540
So to summarize three tips,
do your homework on content,

00:08:09.540 --> 00:08:14.690
have engaging conversations,
have a confident body posture and

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:16.670
mirror the energy level in the room.

00:08:16.670 --> 00:08:19.169
Remember, it starts before it starts.

00:08:21.561 --> 00:08:24.497
Now let's see if Brett has
learned through this process.

